WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:03.779
It's something of an understatement to say
that Warner Bros.' slate of DC films have

00:00:03.779 --> 00:00:04.779
trouble at the theaters.

00:00:04.779 --> 00:00:10.070
Though fans have largely enjoyed the DC Comics
movies and each franchise entry has done relatively

00:00:10.070 --> 00:00:14.440
well at the box office, critics have consistently
ripped the offerings to shreds.

00:00:14.440 --> 00:00:19.890
With the exception of 2017's Wonder Woman,
the DC Extended Universe has really been struggling.

00:00:19.890 --> 00:00:25.150
Marvel, on the other hand, routinely owns
the box office, captivates critics, and holds

00:00:25.150 --> 00:00:28.960
the attention of theatergoers worldwide each
time it rolls out a new film.

00:00:28.960 --> 00:00:34.399
As Avengers: Infinity War proves for the umpteenth
time, the MCU's cavalcade of superheroes has

00:00:34.399 --> 00:00:37.800
a grip on Hollywood that doesn't show any
signs of slowing.

00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:42.230
So, how does one patch up the problems of
the DC Universe, and potentially bring it

00:00:42.230 --> 00:00:43.870
up to Marvel's speed?

00:00:43.870 --> 00:00:48.280
Infinity War screenwriters Christopher Markus
and Stephen McFeely have a simple solution.

00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:53.620
On a recent episode of Kevin Smith's "Fatman
on Batman" podcast, Smith asked the writers:

00:00:53.620 --> 00:00:59.579
"If someone offered you a ton of money and
swayed you to the dark side and said, 'Fix

00:00:59.579 --> 00:01:03.129
these movies,' how would you fix the DC Universe?"

00:01:03.129 --> 00:01:08.590
Markus dished up his no-frills, all-fun filmmaking
game plan: Put the central lineup of DC heroes

00:01:08.590 --> 00:01:13.280
on the shelf for a moment and focus on just
one character at a time rather than the universe

00:01:13.280 --> 00:01:14.280
as a whole.

00:01:14.280 --> 00:01:20.510
"Look at what Marvel did out of necessity,
in that they didn't have their A-list characters.

00:01:20.510 --> 00:01:21.860
They didn't have Spider-Man.

00:01:21.860 --> 00:01:23.530
They didn't have the X-Men."

00:01:23.530 --> 00:01:29.580
Instead, the MCU's opening salvo was Iron
Man, a leading character that might not have

00:01:29.580 --> 00:01:34.480
been the most obvious choice as the godfather
to the entire Marvel Universe, but eventually

00:01:34.480 --> 00:01:35.690
worked out pretty well.

00:01:35.690 --> 00:01:36.730
"He's pretty famous.

00:01:36.730 --> 00:01:37.900
He's Iron Man.

00:01:37.900 --> 00:01:40.760
But he wasn't there.

00:01:40.760 --> 00:01:42.790
And they made a really good movie out of it."

00:01:42.790 --> 00:01:47.550
As for how that applies to the DC Universe,
well, Markus thinks it's all about making

00:01:47.550 --> 00:01:52.580
a few creative character choices there, too,
by giving Superman and Batman some time off,

00:01:52.580 --> 00:01:56.560
and exploring other characters from the comics
that might have some similar appeal.

00:01:56.560 --> 00:02:04.350
"Go through the vast world and go, 'That guy
or that girl,' and go, 'Let's just make a

00:02:04.350 --> 00:02:06.250
really good movie."

00:02:06.250 --> 00:02:11.840
For his part, McFeely also agreed that making
a single film at a time is the way to go.

00:02:11.840 --> 00:02:15.400
"Strategically, 'Make one.

00:02:15.560 --> 00:02:17.840
To quote Justice League, 'Save one person.'"

00:02:17.849 --> 00:02:19.450
Perhaps they're on to something.

00:02:19.450 --> 00:02:24.480
From the studio cooking up a slew of Joker
movies simultaneously, Ben Affleck's flip-flopping

00:02:24.480 --> 00:02:29.709
about whether or not to ditch the Caped Crusader
cowl, and executives mapping out its alternate

00:02:29.709 --> 00:02:33.610
universe movie banner on the side, things
are a bit of a mess down in the DC Universe.

00:02:33.610 --> 00:02:36.749
"There's a lot of spaghetti being thrown at
the wall."

00:02:36.749 --> 00:02:41.019
We can't say for certain whether Markus and
McFeely's proposition is the perfect one to

00:02:41.019 --> 00:02:45.379
save the DC Universe, but slowing down to
stop the spaghetti from sliding off the walls

00:02:45.379 --> 00:02:47.599
and onto the floor sounds like a smart idea.

00:02:47.599 --> 00:02:49.090
Thanks for watching!

00:02:49.090 --> 00:02:51.590
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:02:51.590 --> 00:02:53.659
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

